{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons","id":1483535,"title":"Faith in Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-09T17:56:37-07:00","id":1483535,"title":"Faith in Demons","content":"So, here I am again with another &quot;Hot topic&quot; lol<br /> <br /> This is something I have discussed with players and storytellers alike, since I was a kid, but I don't have a definite answer. What's your thoughts on the issue of someone having True Faith, but for demons, etc? Since I was a kid, I had many players ask for this kind of things when I allowed (I rarely did, but I did it a couple of times in the last 20 years) them to make infernalist characters. What do you think of True Faith for infernalists? Isn't it too broken and kind of &quot;antitematic&quot;? Or would you say it's acceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T18:23:17-07:00","id":1483541,"title":"","content":"It's canon that a businessman can have faith in a copy of an Ayn Rand novel or something like that. So faith in the Devil isn't really a big leap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T19:18:59-07:00","id":1483546,"title":"","content":"So you think it's thematically appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T19:41:42-07:00","id":1483548,"title":"","content":"I think it's awful thematically, not that much worse than some of the in-canon examples though. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd say True Faith requires believing in something without proof of it's existence. So, an infernialist who can summon demons and actually interact with them won't develop it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T19:51:58-07:00","id":1483549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I'd say True Faith requires believing in something without proof of it's existence. So, an infernialist who can summon demons and actually interact with them won't develop it. </div> </div> </div>That's a good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T21:48:55-07:00","id":1483553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483548#post1483548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd say True Faith requires believing in something without proof of it's existence. So, an infernialist who can summon demons and actually interact with them won't develop it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Usually I say this too, but on the other hand - and please allow me to be the Devil's advocate, excuse the pun - to those who Belive, the visions, the gospels, prophecies, the manifestation of angels or Jesus's head on a toast are all proofs<br /> I would say, a good example of &quot;Faith in the Devil&quot; is Grigori Yefimovich Rasputin from Hellboy, whos faith is unquestionable in the Ogdru-Jahad.<br /> His quote is a powerfull one:<br /> \u201cYour God chooses to remain silent. My God lives within me,\u201d Rasputin had said to Trevor Broom right before he had Kroenen kill him.<br /> Rasputin, though he had at one time been a monk, never considered that the silence of this God that Trevor Broom believed in, and had taught Hellboy to believe in, was much, much stronger than the noise of the chaotic, tentacled god that Rasputin was incubating in his own body.<br /> But it wont change the fact, Rasputin Faith was unshakable and very true &quot;Dark Faith&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-10-2022, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T22:11:50-07:00","id":1483555,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think it\u2019s thematically appropriate. True Faith largely grants powers related to repelling supernatural creatures, greater willpower, resisting magic, that sort of thing. That isn\u2019t what you would expect to have from worshipping the Devil. Devil worshippers should get infernal investments or Dark Thaumaturgy, both of which are way more thematic powers than those granted by True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T22:24:51-07:00","id":1483556,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> Aaaand no<br /> As per the Merit:<br /> &quot;You have a deep-seated faith in (and love for) Gaia, God or whatever it is you consider the Almighty. You begin the game with one point of Faith. This Faith provides you with an inner strength and comfort that continues to support you when all else betrays you. The exact effects of Faith can vary from person to person, and some are almost never obvious; some of the most saintly people never perform miracles greater than managing to ease an injured soul's suffering - Even Palpatine saved Anakin's life and kept him alive ^^<br /> \u2022 Any character with Faith may attempt to ward off any supernatural by brandishing a holy symbol or uttering prayers - This obviously could works with &quot;unholy&quot; symbnols too<br /> \u2022\u2022 Any character with a Faith rating of 2 or more may resist supernatural Mind-Control - No problem here with the unholy protection<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 A person with a Faith score of 3 or more may sense the presence of a supernatural. She need not conciously try to sense a supernatural's presence, but must be in peaceful, quiet surroundings - perhaps alone in thought, praying, reading Torah, mediting on the Bible, etc. This ability need not be infallible; GMs should let the character sense the supernatural only if doing so is dramatically appropriate. - like above, no prob here<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The character may not be turned into a ghoul and is unaffected by any mind-altering Disciplines (Presence, Obfuscate, etc.), Gifts and other supernatural powers. - same as above<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The character is so pure, so holy, that she can fill any supernatural with a stunning array of emotion - Obvisously, those would be very dark emotions in this case, ideal for temptation even; open the gates of the soul and heart of others to the darkness of your Dark God. Chutullu say Hello<br /> <br /> I would say yes; plausible. If the GM and the Player could work this out? Sure, why not<br /> Faith have indeed stranger &quot;focus&quot; than the Devil or a particiluar Demon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-10-2022, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T23:55:29-07:00","id":1483560,"title":"","content":"The powers associated with True Faith come from within the faithful mortal, not from on high. Yes, it's absolutely appropriate. Full stop.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that some real world luciferian denominations and demonolatry traditions are quite positive and life-affirming, and there's no reason why comparable traditions wouldn't exist in the World of Darkness. Cults devoted to low Torment Fallen might be well represented among these faith groups where mortals with True Faith can be found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T01:54:49-07:00","id":1483564,"title":"","content":"It depends on which setting and rules you are using. Clanbook Baali and the Mage book &quot;Infernalism: The Path of Screams&quot; have &quot;Infernal Faith&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although some folk would like to deny that such Faith is possible, it infests a small but powerful elite. With it, Black Monks and Queens of Hell defile holy places, menace angels and drive the children of God from their sight. </div> </div> </div>It functions like True Faith, with a caveat that you get the Echoes flaw at level 4 or 5. It also makes you do Highlander throwdown if you meet someone with regular True Faith. The Baali merit melts crosses and gives heart attacks to the priests.<br /> <br /> Conversely, DAV20 disavows such things, demanding that True Faith be in something positive.<br /> <br /> So ultimately, pick what fits narratively. If your game would be improved with dark miracles and subjugation of creatures of the night to a high power - go for it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't really like True Faith effects as written, they are very weapon-y, and that's not what I'm about. My characters call upon true faith to provide support and hope. Or, with Infernal faith - soul-crushing despair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 06-10-2022, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:25:51-07:00","id":1483592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> please allow me to be the Devil's advocate, excuse the pun </div> </div> </div>That was a good one hahaha...<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, you made a good point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, DAV20 disavows such things, demanding that True Faith be in something positive. </div> </div> </div>To be sincere, I didn't even know they officially disavowed it, I think I haven't read this part of V20. <br /> <br /> All in all, I think it's kind of a sensitive topic, there are good arguments both to allow it and not to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:47:19-07:00","id":1483599,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon, yes. By actually lore? No. Turns out in DTF, True Faith is a weapon used by those who believe in God.<br /> <br /> So from the perception of the demons themselves, True Faith is only possible in the hands of the enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:00:44-07:00","id":1483605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483548#post1483548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd say True Faith requires believing in something without proof of it's existence. So, an infernialist who can summon demons and actually interact with them won't develop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd contest that, The prime examples we have for true faith are typically people who have a personal connection with and proof of the entity the had faith in. People like Moses, Jesus, saints etc, were all having full Conversations with god and the angels.<br /> <br /> You have similar situations in non abrahamic religions as well, too the extent that it was considered The Default.<br /> <br /> So I'd say having true faith in something you can't know about is the Opposite of how it works. True faith comes from having a personal relationship with what you believe in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-10-2022, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:23:34-07:00","id":1483610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483605#post1483605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd contest that, The prime examples we have for true faith are typically people who have a personal connection with and proof of the entity the had faith in. People like Moses, Jesus, saints etc, were all having full Conversations with god and the angels.<br /> <br /> You have similar situations in non abrahamic religions as well, too the extent that it was considered The Default.<br /> <br /> So I'd say having true faith in something you can't know about is the Opposite of how it works. True faith comes from having a personal relationship with what you believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting point. One thing to note is that, some guy mentioned that infernalists have Dark Thaumaturgy and Infernal Investments, but I have to say that one has nothing to do with the other, as we see many examples of characters with True Faith AND many other different powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T10:34:47-07:00","id":1483615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483610#post1483610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting point. One thing to note is that, some guy mentioned that infernalists have Dark Thaumaturgy and Infernal Investments, but I have to say that one has nothing to do with the other, as we see many examples of characters with True Faith AND many other different powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True Faith comes from unevering belief, devotion and dedication to your deity. It's actually of form of fanaticism.<br /> <br /> Dark Thaumaturgy is just practical occult knowledge with demonic orign, and infernal investments are the pay from pacts. You could have both even if you secretly despises and wants the downfall of your devil benefactor.<br /> <br /> So yes, I do think that Dark True Faith is possible. Im not well versed in V5 or the newer editions of M20, but it was present in both older editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T11:26:44-07:00","id":1483619,"title":"","content":"Given that devils and gods are pretty interchangeable in the WoD, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:02:22-07:00","id":1483629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483615#post1483615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True Faith comes from unevering belief, devotion and dedication to your deity. It's actually of form of fanaticism.<br /> <br /> Dark Thaumaturgy is just practical occult knowledge with demonic orign, and infernal investments are the pay from pacts. You could have both even if you secretly despises and wants the downfall of your devil benefactor.<br /> <br /> So yes, I do think that Dark True Faith is possible. Im not well versed in V5 or the newer editions of M20, but it was present in both older editions</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, all in all I don't see any reason not to allow it, besides aesthetic preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T00:03:12-07:00","id":1483695,"title":"","content":"In general the problem with True Faith is its specific set of associated powers.<br /> <br /> Faith is a complex sentiment, and can be tied to anything. A religion, philosophy, group, idea, it doesn't matter, and in its original write-up the True Faith trait recognizes this. Being positive or negative is also an extremely narrow view of theology. To me that should put the Society of Leopold right away without TF, because I can't conceive their Fire and Brimstone style of Catholicism as positive. And there are people with pretty humanitarian views through the veneration of demons.<br /> <br /> But the actual powers of True Faith given are all <b>heavily</b> based on Christian imagery and stories. They make perfect sense from a Christian POV, but for other beliefs they seem really off, you either need some (or a lot of) effort to even justify them, or they simply make no sense for that belief system.<br /> <br /> So, while for the concept I think it is a perfectly acceptable option and may be quite thematic depending on the chronicle and the character, in practice it is the rules that may fail you and give inappropriate effects. You would either have to carefully consider this faith for the powers to make sense for the character's belief, or you would have to tweak True Faith itself to offer more adequate benefits.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, it has nothing to do with the &quot;positive belief&quot; nonsense. Take for example the very first power, the ability to ward off Vampires. A believer In Candombl\u00e9 would possibly make a ritual offering for the Orisha to request protection for the rest of the week. A Muslim could recite the word of Allah to force the Kindred to follow suit and respect them as Faithful, but for neither does it make any sense to brandish something and just pray to make vampires step back, it just doesn't make a lot of sense for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T01:46:15-07:00","id":1483706,"title":"","content":"I believe some attempt at emulation important in the World of Darkness. It is supposed to be our world through a mirror darkly. So if you depart too much, it's not the WoD but some kind of fantasy world only vaguely similar to ours.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, I only allow True Faith for the monotheistic religions, although I would allow something similar for Buddhism that is flavor texted appropriately. There's enough real world folktales and legends that show Buddhist monks and such doing <i>similar</i> enough things.<br /> <br /> For the historical pagan religions I'd allow appropriate Paths of Sorcery to reflect what myths and legends allow for them. If you want Isis to protect you, better find an actual priestess of Isis who knows the Path of Enchantment so she can craft a protective amulet for you.<br /> <br /> I'd never use it for any kind of demon worship. That's we why we have Infernalism and their infernal investments and appropriate Dark Thaumaturgy and Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Almost every religion has some tradition of bestowing the blessing or protection of the divine against supernatural evil. It's just a matter of what best emulates it.<br /> <br /> When it comes to religious &quot;magic&quot; or miracles, I don't believe in doubling up. If the person's &quot;powers&quot; are best emulated by something like a Path of Sorcery or some other Numina, you don't get True Faith. I even hold this for the monotheists. If a Christian NPC has some kind of Theurgy, I don't think they should have True Faith. If you are attempting to <i>control</i> forces beyond mortal ability, you're not allowing yourself to become a vessel for the Almighty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T10:50:30-07:00","id":1483726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483706#post1483706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to religious &quot;magic&quot; or miracles, I don't believe in doubling up. If the person's &quot;powers&quot; are best emulated by something like a Path of Sorcery or some other Numina, you don't get True Faith. I even hold this for the monotheists. If a Christian NPC has some kind of Theurgy, I don't think they should have True Faith. If you are attempting to <i>control</i> forces beyond mortal ability, you're not allowing yourself to become a vessel for the Almighty.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that those other belief systems aren't necessarily best represented by a Path or other Numina.<br /> <br /> What is True Faith? It is the power of your conviction producing effects by channeling the might of the deity instead of your own.<br /> <br /> For the Candombl\u00e9 and many other religions the offering ritual isn't about knowing complex ritae or being special. They <b>do</b> have priests with special powers and knowledge, they have mediums, but making an offering for protection is something simple that any faithful can do, and the Orisha will favor a more fervent faithful despite knowledge and personal &quot;powers&quot;. For the Muslim the word of God applies to everyone equally, there's no demons and angels in the way Christians think, as an irredeemable race, and more than any generic power, the word of God is <b>law</b> in the technical sense. Anyone can recite the Quran to remind the Djinns and other monsters of the Law and the protection afforded to the Faithful, be those monsters Shay\u0101tin or not.<br /> <br /> All those and many other aspects of many belief systems do not translate well to other Numina just because their actions seem so from the POV of an outsider. They're not special techniques where faith plays just a minor role in, they're not secret knowledge or the power of an initiate in the mysteries or in the priesthood. They're legends about the power of the divine when channeled through conviction by the faithful, regardless of education, holiness or caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T10:55:07-07:00","id":1483727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483726#post1483726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that those other belief systems aren't necessarily best represented by a Path or other Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, almost every religion has some tradition of bestowing the blessing or protection of the divine against supernatural evil. It's just a matter of what best emulates it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T11:38:40-07:00","id":1483734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483695#post1483695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being positive or negative is also an extremely narrow view of theology. To me that should put the Society of Leopold right away without TF, because I can't conceive their Fire and Brimstone style of Catholicism as positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you are conflating the terms here. &quot;Positive&quot; here means a faith that believes in the inherent goodness and benevolence of the deity for the world at large. It's not about &quot;nice&quot; effects or being friendly to an individual. It's about opposing existential evil with faith. And in DAV20, it requires a near-death experience brought by the supernatural. &quot;Vampires stalk the night preying on the innocent and my faith smites them&quot; is positive.<br /> <br /> That said, my opinion is that the Society of Leopold ran like the Vatican Gestapo shouldn't have True Faith to begin with.<br /> <br /> Also, I personally don't like to generalize systems world-wide. Cultural beliefs are so diverse that creating Unified Theory Of Faith just leaves you with the Purple Magic Paradigm equivalent. If I run a game set in the US then Christianity is objectively correct and YHVH is true, and I don't care what that says about the pagans. You aren't meeting any, it's not relevant to the story. And vice versa - I don't care about the implications of a Buddhist horror story on the Christian theology, the story isn't about the Christians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T13:55:11-07:00","id":1483743,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of flavour, obviously, and of taste. I gotta say that &quot;Dark&quot; True Faith has a heavy D&amp;D flavour in it, influence of the idea of &quot;Evil Clerics&quot;. D&amp;D doesnt have True Faith, but it has Clerical Spells - which you could say that is the game mechanic for it. So, in a sense, this wouldnt be a new concept in RPG.<br /> <br /> That being said, for OTHER systems and games, as is the case of WoD that has this is a particular trait with particular mechanics that dont ressemble D&amp;D's spells lists, it is largely a matter of taste. If you want your &quot;evil clerics&quot; to have that particular mechanic, do it. If however, for your view of the setting this isnt a good fit, dont. I wouldnt set this on stone either way.<br /> <br /> In my own view of the setting, I make True Faith to be a sort of &quot;Magik&quot; with K, that is, it comes from the Avatar, just like Spheres from Mages, except that it works is if a sort of &quot;sleep-walking&quot; ability rather than true magik. That's why I allow it to... Anyone. I even allow it for someone that believes utterly and fanatically in the &quot;power of the Computer&quot;... If anyone like that existed and were REALLY capable of developing a personal connection that goes in an absolute metaphysical way with their laptop, I would in theory allow it... But sure, that's MY take on it, because my WoD is an animistic one, sure, supernatural too, but ultimately an atheistic one... I have no &quot;God&quot; running the show (just a few occasional powerful beings that title themselves &quot;gods&quot;, but that doesnt make them the cosmic rulers of all).<br /> <br /> So, each ST just do as best serves them in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T13:56:34-07:00","id":1483744,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the typing errors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T14:41:46-07:00","id":1483748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483743#post1483743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of flavour, obviously, and of taste. I gotta say that &quot;Dark&quot; True Faith has a heavy D&amp;D flavour in it, influence of the idea of &quot;Evil Clerics&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the idea of &quot;satanists&quot;(I use the term loosely hear) are as old as counter-culture, which is only slightly younger than Culture is.<br /> <br /> Religious teachings tend to have the issue of being limited to the imagination and wisdom of the peoples practicing them, which leads to them very easily going in unintended directions. An example of this are some denominations of Gnosticism which 100% believed that the Old testimate god was the enemy and that lucifer was the guiding hand trying to save us.<br /> <br /> There are also very real religions centered around very brutal gods that Demanded things like regular human sacrifice. An example: huitzilopochtli the sun god of the aztec empire required regular sacrifices of human blood to give him the strength to fight off the Tzitzimime/Tzitzimitl, monstrous skeleton goddesses who shone in the night as the stars and would eat the world if the sun god fell in battle. The aztecs were Very much labeled as demon worship by the christian conquistadors at the time(partly to justify their own actions).<br /> <br /> &quot;Demon worship&quot; as a concept is much, Much older than D&amp;D. It's just another concept they aped in creating the modern &quot;Standard Fantasy Setting&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T15:41:03-07:00","id":1483752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483734#post1483734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you are conflating the terms here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not.<br /> <br /> To me a version of Christianity that promotes a vengeful God that condones the extermination of a class of &quot;monsters&quot; without even admitting the possibility of redemption and follows a God so merciful He will condemn every non-believer to either oblivion or suffering upon death, is a religion dedicated to objective, existential evil. And many believers of satanist churches believe the Christian theology is propaganda by an evil &quot;God&quot; and that their patrons are inherently good and benevolent, not only to them, but to the world at large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483734#post1483734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cultural beliefs are so diverse that creating Unified Theory Of Faith just leaves you with the Purple Magic Paradigm equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think True Faith should do what it says it does, model the effects of Faith in a setting where it has metaphysical weight. I don't think it should do everything, I think it should be versatile enough to give options within this framework, instead of forcing STs and players to resort to other frameworks equally or more inadequate, but that do not even claim to do the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483734#post1483734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I run a game set in the US then Christianity is objectively correct and YHVH is true, and I don't care what that says about the pagans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly your right, but it isn't what the game claims to cover and isn't an argument for people that are specifically declaring they want to run a game under other premises. The OP is about what can be done with the mechanical trait True Faith, not what can be done with the mechanical trait True Faith under the premise that the Christians are Right and every other faith is objectively false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T20:04:56-07:00","id":1483771,"title":"","content":"A note about true faiths effects, the level one power doesn't rejects enemies condemned by the faithful(if that were true there would be a lot of minorities suffering from magic splash damage).<br /> <br /> Faith seems to mainly Affect creatures that the God Itself would have issue with. The heavily christian-centric true faith presented in WOD repels vampires, demons, and ghosts that refuse to pass on, but it doesn't actually harm mages or werewolves for example. One of the books has it that True Faith prevents Garou from using Rage or shape-shifting, but Gnosis gifts are fine. People with true faith can resist or dispell True magick, but the mage themselves is left untouched and they don't suffer any paradox related effects.<br /> <br /> This might suggest that the god of the true-faith user only intervenes to protect their faithful most of the time, and only goes out of their way to hurt things that are already on it's kill list. A non-abrahamic faith might not be harmful to demons(though still protecting the faithful from demonic magic like vs a sphere mage) simply because that god doesn't recognize demons as &quot;evil&quot; so much as part of how the world is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T11:24:56-07:00","id":1483891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483748#post1483748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, the idea of &amp;quot;satanists&amp;quot;(I use the term loosely hear) are as old as counter-culture, which is only slightly younger than Culture is.<br /> <br /> Religious teachings tend to have the issue of being limited to the imagination and wisdom of the peoples practicing them, which leads to them very easily going in unintended directions. An example of this are some denominations of Gnosticism which 100% believed that the Old testimate god was the enemy and that lucifer was the guiding hand trying to save us.<br /> <br /> There are also very real religions centered around very brutal gods that Demanded things like regular human sacrifice. An example: huitzilopochtli the sun god of the aztec empire required regular sacrifices of human blood to give him the strength to fight off the Tzitzimime/Tzitzimitl, monstrous skeleton goddesses who shone in the night as the stars and would eat the world if the sun god fell in battle. The aztecs were Very much labeled as demon worship by the christian conquistadors at the time(partly to justify their own actions).<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Demon worship&amp;quot; as a concept is much, Much older than D&amp;D. It's just another concept they aped in creating the modern &amp;quot;Standard Fantasy Setting&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im sorry, I didnt made myself clear. As much as what you're saying is true, the faith of neither one of those people ever created miracles... Unless you're a believer of course. And I also include muslims, christians or any others in that too. So, &quot;True Faith&quot; as a source of &quot;magic&quot; powers doesnt exist in the real world. At least for a skeptic atheist such as myself - I have no trouble for believers that think otherwise.<br /> <br /> What I was meaning was in terms of RPG mechanics, not real life cultures. And in terms of RPG, the idea of believe in the divine granting you magic powers in terms of game mechanics comes from D&amp;D, and in that it didnt matter if the source was &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T11:40:39-07:00","id":1483893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483752#post1483752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not.<br /> <br /> To me a version of Christianity that promotes a vengeful God that condones the extermination of a class of &amp;quot;monsters&amp;quot; without even admitting the possibility of redemption and follows a God so merciful He will condemn every non-believer to either oblivion or suffering upon death, is a religion dedicated to objective, existential evil. And many believers of satanist churches believe the Christian theology is propaganda by an evil &amp;quot;God&amp;quot; and that their patrons are inherently good and benevolent, not only to them, but to the world at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, monoteistic religions are... Kind of terrible in that regard. There are some merits to it, but also many negatives.<br /> <br /> I give it a discount given that those religions were create by ancient and imperfect humans who didnt know any better - and yet, they tried. I dont subject history to visions of villains/heroes. If today with the internet giving more knowledge at the palm of my hands than the entire library of Alexandria we still havent managed to create a &quot;perfect world&quot; - because there is no such thing - I cannot judge our ancestors based on the world of today.<br /> <br /> I gotta say thou, the best religions were Zoroatrism and Janaism. Those were much better than the others. Which is why they ended up being smashed by worse ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483752#post1483752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think True Faith should do what it says it does, model the effects of Faith in a setting where it has metaphysical weight. I don't think it should do everything, I think it should be versatile enough to give options within this framework, instead of forcing STs and players to resort to other frameworks equally or more inadequate, but that do not even claim to do the job.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's certainly your right, but it isn't what the game claims to cover and isn't an argument for people that are specifically declaring they want to run a game under other premises. The OP is about what can be done with the mechanical trait True Faith, not what can be done with the mechanical trait True Faith under the premise that the Christians are Right and every other faith is objectively false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I equate True Faith in WoD as a sort of &quot;Uncouncious Awaken Magik&quot; in my headcanon, instead of &quot;divine intervention&quot;. But that's me of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T12:57:07-07:00","id":1483901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483891#post1483891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im sorry, I didnt made myself clear. As much as what you're saying is true, the faith of neither one of those people ever created miracles... Unless you're a believer of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I'm talking about though Wod isn't a simulation of real life, it's a game where folktales and cheesy 90's movies are adapted as True(plus some extra). The various vampire disciplines represent actual IRL vampire myths and folklore. The actual representation of vampires and their basic non-discipline abilities are taken from the 90's movie vampire inspired from ann rice books.<br /> <br /> True faith as it originally appeared in VTM was a power representing tropes and myths surounding vampire movies.<br /> <br /> Similarly Demonic true faith is based on applying the WoD take on true faith more broadly than it's christian-cebtric roots, which has grounds in both folklore in the myth of demon worsgippers And in movies. D&amp;D has nothing to do with it at any angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T23:22:12-07:00","id":1483964,"title":"","content":"I generally state that True Faith can only exist in a divine entity of some sort.<br /> <br /> Setites believe passionately in Set but don't have True Faith because Set is a vampire not a god.<br /> <br /> I admit I do have a House Rule for True Faith in my games, though. Which is that True Faith in my games is a form of Numina not a merit. You buy True Faith as a skill and maintain it with a 1-5 level.<br /> <br /> I feel it much better serves the uses of it to treat it like a form of hedge magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T23:55:24-07:00","id":1483966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally state that True Faith can only exist in a divine entity of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't necessarily solve the question because demons are arguably divine entities of some sort. That depends a lot on how you interpret divine entity, the setting and the nature of demons (or the demons you're talking about).<br /> <br /> Can a Bane Incarna be considered a divine being? What if they're a Totem? Is a Fallen or an Earthbound a divine being? They're direct divine creations with the power and purpose to shape the world, as they did it in the beginning. What about the Hsien, the Little Gods? By all accounts they're exactly that, small in their power and standing, but still gods in the Heavenly Hierarchy. If a Setite does achieve Gnostic Enlightenment, ascending to the level of the Aeons, will this be a divine person? What about an Oracle? If you attain the status of Yama King, are you divine by virtue of your place and standing in the Cosmic Order, despite your nature?<br /> <br /> Not that I think your take isn't valid. It isn't <b>canon</b>, but is certainly valid. But it does raise a lot more hard questions than it seems at first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T08:44:47-07:00","id":1483987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally state that True Faith can only exist in a divine entity of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>In here I have to admit that I let my personal atheist bias take the hold of my view of the setting.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that &quot;God&quot; or &quot;The One&quot; or whatever is a Deistic entity if it exists at all, therefore he doesnt answer prayers in my games.<br /> <br /> And other &quot;Deities&quot; arent true &quot;gods&quot;, just &quot;powerful beings&quot; - be it a powerful spirit like Gaia or any such.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, those &quot;gods&quot; are just what lesser beings call them, but they are &quot;gods&quot; just in the same way as the Marvel Thor is a &quot;god&quot; too - a powerful being which mere mortals attribute divinity to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setites believe passionately in Set but don't have True Faith because Set is a vampire not a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... A good point. And a massive punch on my stomach, ouch!<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, I know it, Setites believe in their &quot;power of the blood&quot;, therefore they dont develop True Faith in Set because they believe that their &quot;gifts&quot; from Set come from their disciplines! Yes, life is good again! Yay!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it much better serves the uses of it to treat it like a form of hedge magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that treatment too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-14-2022, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:58:56-07:00","id":1484000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483987#post1483987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... A good point. And a massive punch on my stomach, ouch!</div> </div> </div> </div>By the rules, there's nothing that actually impedes a Setite from having True Faith if you want that.<br /> <br /> True Faith is deemed rare, first because it takes humongous levels of faith, not just &quot;much&quot;. A lot of people are really, truly devout to their religions and that still doesn't give them True Faith. And second because True Faith represents a particular way of expressing this Faith, it is the ability to ward evil and perform miracles, which isn't exactly the same as performing magic, so even a person with enough faith to have it may not have the inclination to act as needed to wield it.<br /> <br /> A Catholic priest with enough Faith that is happy with his place in the Lord's plan as a servant and minister will have zero reasons to ever try to do anything like the powers of True Faith, and so probably won't have it as a trait and won't ever use it if he has.<br /> <br /> Yet, it doesn't means you can't have a Setite character that has it, not any Setite Sorcery, but actual True Faith being wielded in the name of Set. Nothing against it in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T13:28:34-07:00","id":1484034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally state that True Faith can only exist in a divine entity of some sort.<br /> <br /> Setites believe passionately in Set but don't have True Faith because Set is a vampire not a god.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483987#post1483987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... A good point. And a massive punch on my stomach, ouch!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> There is however a Counter-point: Due to some rules weirdness that I don't think was updated, Vampires specifically are banned from having true faith unless they have a humanity of 9+. What self-respecting setite has path of humanity, let alone at nine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T15:55:22-07:00","id":1484052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484034#post1484034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point.<br /> <br /> There is however a Counter-point: Due to some rules weirdness that I don't think was updated, Vampires specifically are banned from having true faith unless they have a humanity of 9+. What self-respecting setite has path of humanity, let alone at nine?</div> </div> </div> </div>To undercut myself, Moncada has True Faith despite being a child molesting Path of Night Complete Monster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:24:06-07:00","id":1484058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484052#post1484052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To undercut myself, Moncada has True Faith despite being a child molesting Path of Night Complete Monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this said rule of &quot;only vampires with humanity 9+&quot; wasn't introduced in every book, to be sincere I don't even remember where I read it, but you see many cainite characters who have Faith and have a lower humanity than 9. Hell! Not even Sulivan Dane has Humanity 9, which means not even humans have such a high rating of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:35:30-07:00","id":1484059,"title":"","content":"Irrc, didn't they give an example of a businessman having faith in an Ayn Rand book or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T17:36:18-07:00","id":1484067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484052#post1484052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To undercut myself, Moncada has True Faith despite being a child molesting Path of Night Complete Monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484058#post1484058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this said rule of &quot;only vampires with humanity 9+&quot; wasn't introduced in every book, to be sincere I don't even remember where I read it, but you see many cainite characters who have Faith and have a lower humanity than 9. Hell! Not even Sulivan Dane has Humanity 9, which means not even humans have such a high rating of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>True faith has required Humanity 9+ since it was added as a supernatural Merit in revised. It's specified in the Merit for both the <b>Vampire Revised</b> and <b>V20</b> <b>Core Books</b>.<br /> <br /> Though, that has never stopped White Wolf from making NPCs that break the rules they themselves wrote. WW is unfortunately notorious for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:10:42-07:00","id":1484073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1483964#post1483964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally state that True Faith can only exist in a divine entity of some sort.<br /> <br /> Setites believe passionately in Set but don't have True Faith because Set is a vampire not a god.<br /> <br /> I admit I do have a House Rule for True Faith in my games, though. Which is that True Faith in my games is a form of Numina not a merit. You buy True Faith as a skill and maintain it with a 1-5 level.<br /> <br /> I feel it much better serves the uses of it to treat it like a form of hedge magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that True Faith in the Christian God would also require that you abide by the precepts of that God. Therefore, a child molesting monster like Moncada would be too much of a habitual sinner to ever develop True Faith no matter what the books say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:26:28-07:00","id":1484077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484067#post1484067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True faith has required Humanity 9+ since it was added as a supernatural Merit in revised. It's specified in the Merit for both the <b>Vampire Revised</b> and <b>V20</b> <b>Core Books</b>.<br /> <br /> Though, that has never stopped White Wolf from making NPCs that break the rules they themselves wrote. WW is unfortunately notorious for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With all due respect, as it's such a stupid requirement, I really don't mind them &quot;breaking the rules&quot;, in any case Feroux having Faith 9 is perhaps the most blatant example of how ridiculous is this rule...<br /> <br /> I don't really mind &quot;bad people&quot; having True Faith, I just don't quite like the idea of Faith in Demons...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:28:21-07:00","id":1484078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really mind &quot;bad people&quot; having True Faith </div> </div> </div>Especially because if we stop to think, most people who are supposed to have True Faith are kind of assholes, just think about the usual hunter, like the fabled Van Helsing himself or really, any ordinary inquisitor...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T04:20:55-07:00","id":1484101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484078#post1484078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially because if we stop to think, most people who are supposed to have True Faith are kind of assholes, just think about the usual hunter, like the fabled Van Helsing himself or really, any ordinary inquisitor...</div> </div> </div> </div>What you talking about? Van Helsing is a cool asshole!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T08:11:10-07:00","id":1484110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484059#post1484059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irrc, didn't they give an example of a businessman having faith in an Ayn Rand book or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is ridiculous and I feel thematically inappropriate.<br /> <br /> Unless Vampires are just repulsed by, &quot;Really really strong ideas.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can buy someone having True Faith in a god that doesn't exist or has created himself but I doubt someone can burn someone with an Optimus Prime figure like in BILL THE VAMPIRE (a fantastic book, btw).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484078#post1484078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially because if we stop to think, most people who are supposed to have True Faith are kind of assholes, just think about the usual hunter, like the fabled Van Helsing himself or really, any ordinary inquisitor...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I also like the Inquisition habitually suffers loss of true faith and purges when the evil they do comes back to bite them.<br /> <br /> That is actually a cool story.<br /> <br /> Remember Castlevania's Netflix cartoon? The High Priest laughs at the demons invading the town and says God will protect him. The demon doesn't say God doesn't exist or is powerless. No, he says specifically the priest DISGUSTS God and that he has withdrawn his protection for the fact they're a bunch of murderous assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2022, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T10:19:42-07:00","id":1484114,"title":"","content":"WoD's God is... enigmatic to say the least<br /> We have a few candidates of the title of God<br /> First, there is Jehovah, brother of Lucifer, strongest and first of the Eloihm, other gods, who made Gardens and Lilith visited all of them, and enjoyed an extensive sequence of affairs both of Jehova and Lucifer. This &quot;God&quot; cursed Lilith to never know the love of another. In turn each being that Lilith truly loved and cared for, could never really love her in return. Cursed Lucifer, cursed Adam and Eve and lastly cursed himself. Acoording Revelations of the Dark Mother<br /> Second of our list of Gods is the Creator from Demon: the Fallen. Strangley, while is it widely claimed the Elohim personally knew their Creator, in truth very few actually talked with it, and knew personally, he comunicated thrugh the First House, primely Lucifer, who was the First and told everyone of the Creator's plan. The ones who went to talk to the Creator was never seen or heard of again... weird, huh? Then when the Sebettu escaped...? No God. No Elohim guards to hunt them down. Another widely belived about this one it either left Creation after touched it to toss down on the road of Entropy to make another from another segment of the Abyss (remember, the whole creation was the work of the Elohim, the House of Fundament, they went deep in the Abyss, everything that is NOt God, mined that substance and crafted a perfect little pearl out of it, with all the potential, and after that expanded rapidly &quot;exploded&quot;, that created the known universe, space where the work then begun... a place that is not the Infinite eg. Everything and nor the Abyss eg. Nothing) far from this one, or dead.<br /> Strangley, Days of Fire claims - or at least Lucifer thinks - the Scarlet Queen (or Scarlet Phoneix, based on the lore of the Fallen, is also identified as Ziana, the Seraph of the Cycle, ruler of the Sixth House of angels) and Ebon Dragon are the last remaining Angels on Earth - They are probably the &quot;Messengers&quot; responsible for creating the imbued, or at least the leaders of the factions championing the virtues of Zeal and Mercy. As the Scarlet Queen represents Yang, the active principle, she would represent Zeal. The best of both principles were used to create the Vision creeds). Wich is actually... fitting if we consider, the Scarlet Phoneix and the Ebon Dragon created the Wan Xian, the &quot;original&quot; Hunters of the world, to defend it from the Yama Kings and Demons...<br /> And this leads to our 3rd and probably most likely candidate, the August Personage of Jade from Kindred of the East, Changeling (via Land of 8 million dreams, tho the Little Gods are not really changelings per se), Hunter (via Demon Hunter X), Mage (via Dragons of the East)... a really active God, strongest Minister of the Celestial Bureaucracy, with a strange sense of humor and someone whom the little gods and Yama Kings knew personally - the oldest remember the strange smile on the August Personage's face when He turned away from them, and the wisest suspect that ultimately, they are the butt of a joke which will only be apparent at the end of time. The Sixth Age is near, and when it dawns, the August Personage of Jade stps down of his throne and the Demon Empeor takes it... till the Demon Emperor is beaten, wich signals the arrival of the Seventh Age when things starts to be better, untilly the Wheel of Ages reach the 12th age, wich is the 1st, when everything is One.<br /> All and all, I don't think for True Faith you actually need a &quot;God&quot; to exist or be bothered about your faith<br /> It is something that comes from inside of you... thus the focus of your Faith could be anyhing even.... yeah, an Anna Rice Novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-15-2022, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T13:51:22-07:00","id":1484134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484110#post1484110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can buy someone having True Faith in a god that doesn't exist or has created himself but I doubt someone can burn someone with an Optimus Prime figure like in BILL THE VAMPIRE (a fantastic book, btw).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what they represent for their fans, I'd say that while obviously out of place for VtM, burning a vampire with an action figure of Optimus Prime or Superman is actually more thematically appropriate than an Ayn Rand book.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I do find it interesting to explore the idea of the faithful losing power because they actually let pride and prejudice corrupt their belief and degenerate their actions into evil. But I also think this can be achieved either by having the power of True Faith come from an actual divine entity or by simply stating that at this point their confidence became less about Faith and more about Pride without their realizing.<br /> <br /> Think about Claude Frollo, either in the original script or in the Disney movie: he is extremely devout and dedicated, yet you can easily say his faith became less about God and more about <b>his</b> own moral superiority, no matter how much he desperately seeks divine help when finding his morality lacking (in his own, twisted standards).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484114#post1484114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling (via Land of 8 million dreams, tho the Little Gods are not really changelings per se)</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally strongly think the Hsien work far better as a Demon subsplat than Changeling, they're basically Loyalist Angels that got to be bound to Earth some time after the Fall, through another process. A lot of Demon concepts are already present on them and they're more easily likened to Demon than they ever were to Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:10:56-07:00","id":1484168,"title":"","content":"Im gonna start repeling Vampires with my Mises books. &quot;Begone, foul servant of the State! I shall free the Markets from your unholy interference!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:42:55-07:00","id":1484174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484168#post1484168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im gonna start repeling Vampires with my Mises books. &quot;Begone, foul servant of the State! I shall free the Markets from your unholy interference!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected. This character concept is pure gold!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T22:35:41-07:00","id":1484177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484134#post1484134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally strongly think the Hsien work far better as a Demon subsplat than Changeling, they're basically Loyalist Angels that got to be bound to Earth some time after the Fall, through another process. A lot of Demon concepts are already present on them and they're more easily likened to Demon than they ever were to Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, totally agree!<br /> I mean they have 0 connection to the Dreaming for start<br /> The Shinma are, at their nature, celestial bureaucrats. Their main duty was to record the prayer of a mortal (not only restricted to humans, but also including animals and plants), delegate it to their superiors, the Chi Ling, who then would present the affair before the dragons. These dragons would then decide the matter or turn to the August Personage in Jade for a final verdict. Then, the process reversed, with the Hsien being informed of Heaven's wishes and instructed to act accordingly<br /> Not to mention, many Shinma/Hsien rebelled against their position in the Celestial Bureaucracy, either to help mortals or turn against them, during the terrible events of the Dragon River War. As a result, they were punished by the August Personage in Jade. Those who had dared to place themselves in the position of the Wan Xian were cast out and forced to live among the mortals of the Middle Kingdom. Originally, they were without much protection from chi-leeching enemies until Hanuman managed to find a way back to Heaven and shared his knowledge of balance among the little gods. In the Fifth Age, the hsien are cut off from much of their power, unable to enter the spirit realms, and must cloak themselves in the flesh of mortals. Factionalised and uncertain, some seek to answer mortal prayers without the aid of the bureaucracy of heaven, while others seek selfish dominion over humans or even to destroy the world, allying themselves with the Yama Kings as an act of revenge for their exile.<br /> I mean they were the Fallen, as you said, before the Fallen were inveted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T23:09:10-07:00","id":1484180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484177#post1484177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean they were the Fallen, as you said, before the Fallen were inveted!</div> </div> </div> </div>The only differences, and that actually makes them even easier to include in Demon, is that they're not bound to the Abyss (DtF) and aren't formally removed from the Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> So, if you place the events of the Rebellion before the ages that would culminate in the fall of the Wan Xian, then it is easy to picture the Little Gods as surviving Loyalists, their punishment being a result of the events of a later age.<br /> <br /> And keeping in mind that the source we have for the number of Elohim at Creation states them at about 9 <b>million</b>. If the Hsien were a 1/10th of this, they would be the most numerous Major splat, more than 1 for every 10 thousand humans today, and this is not an improbable number. That's not to argue that those numbers are reliable, but just that as far as we know the idea of the entire splat being the remnants of the original Elohim after so much stuff happening still isn't far-fetched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T03:33:18-07:00","id":1484196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484180#post1484180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And keeping in mind that the source we have for the number of Elohim at Creation states them at about 9 <b>million</b>. If the Hsien were a 1/10th of this, they would be the most numerous Major splat, more than 1 for every 10 thousand humans today, and this is not an improbable number. That's not to argue that those numbers are reliable, but just that as far as we know the idea of the entire splat being the remnants of the original Elohim after so much stuff happening still isn't far-fetched.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hsien might not be 1/10th of the total 9 million Elohim if we're making that connection, they could be 1/10th of the remaining 6 million after 1/3rd were kicked into the abyss at the conclusion of the war in heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T06:08:18-07:00","id":1484204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484174#post1484174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand corrected. This character concept is pure gold!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just imagine a Syndicate Techie Boy with True Faith in the power of the free markets... It's a World of Comic Darkness after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T07:31:40-07:00","id":1484208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483535-faith-in-demons?p=1484196#post1484196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hsien might not be 1/10th of the total 9 million Elohim if we're making that connection, they could be 1/10th of the remaining 6 million after 1/3rd were kicked into the abyss at the conclusion of the war in heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I was considering this already and still being conservative.<br /> <br /> According to Days of Fire, the DtF book that gives the numbers we have, penned in-character by Lucifer (take with a grain of salt), from a little more than 6 million Loyalist Angels, 1 million perished in the war, which means still 5 million survivors. 900 thousands is actually a conservative number, less than a fifth of them being turned into the Hsien. While I wouldn't go so far, it is actually possible to have most of them becoming Hsien, making for about 5 million Little Gods (the precise numbers given make for a little more than 5 thousand beyond the million mark, more than enough to cover <b>all</b> positions in the Umbra we still want to give to Angels), which would be about 1 for each 16 hundred humans today.<br /> <br /> Those numbers may be too big or actually too low depending on how you read the lore, the setting and mythologies in general through the lens of it. But hence the Fallen as a splat on Earth are just an undisclosed fraction of their numbers in Hell, and the Loyalists are consistently said to have been double their numbers, deriving another entire splat from them isn't too much of a stretch anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}